course: dictionary
lesson: 5674
title: Same sound, different meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words look or sound alike, so the context tells you which meaning is right. «The llama carried the heavy sacks up the mountain path.» The clues are carried, sacks and mountain path, so a llama must be an animal that carries loads.
explain: Now read this: «The lama blessed the monks in the temple.» The clues are monks and temple, so a lama must be a Buddhist teacher. Only one letter changes between the two words, so always check the spelling and the context together.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If «The animal blessed the monks in the temple» makes no sense, then lama is not the animal. Check the clues first, then the spelling.
fact: A llama is an animal from South America, with a long neck and a thick woolly coat.
fact: A llama has no hump, so it looks a bit like a small camel.
fact: Llamas are kept for carrying loads and for their wool.
fact: Llamas live in herds in the Andes, and they may spit when they are annoyed.
fact: A lama (one l) is a Buddhist teacher, so it is a different word from llama.
exercise: «The llama carried the sacks up the mountain path.» What is the llama doing? | Writing a letter | Singing to the children | *Carrying loads | Swimming in a lake
exercise: «Llamas live in herds in the Andes.» What is a herd? | *A group of animals living together | A kind of woolly coat | A mountain path | A single animal on its own
exercise: «The lama blessed the monks in the temple.» Who is the lama in this sentence? | An animal that carries loads | A woolly jumper | *A Buddhist teacher | A type of mountain path
test: «Llamas and alpacas were bred in the Andes to carry loads and to give soft wool.» What were llamas bred for? | *Carrying loads and giving wool | Swimming in the sea | Being pets only in London | Racing in the Olympics
test: Ruby's gran knitted her a jumper with a purple llama on it. What is a llama? | *A South American animal with a long neck and woolly coat | A kind of hat | A fruit from the Andes | A Buddhist teacher
exam: Which spelling means a Buddhist teacher? | llamas | llamma | *lama | llama
